{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Jacob was left alone.</b> Rashi explains: this teaches that he remained for small flasks, and he based this on the fact that it is written לבדו — do not read לבדו but rather לכדו (to his flask). Another explanation: it is the language of בית הבד (an olive press) from which one draws olive oil, and it is customary to store oil in small flasks."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:24.399517812Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}